<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law (Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation))",
        "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law faithfully reproduces Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs",
        "reported_in_source: Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph",
        "reported_in_source: Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01)",
        "reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis",
        "transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv; output: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png; organism: Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9; artifact_sha256: d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=c22c5f4e26f3e2c6...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-18-venation-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs; transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks; does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-7> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 9.13e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Code-to-model traceability: 94/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every equation is linked to both Python implementation lines and non-vacuous machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean (Section 13: parameterized ObeysMurrayLaw gamma induction, strict RNG lune equivalence, and planar cycle/edge-deletion theorems, 0 sorrys, 0 warnings). Evidence: morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean L361–L443: Section 13 formal Lean 4 theorems (murray_1926_tree_conservation, runions_2005_rng_lune_iff, katifori_2012_edge_deletion_merges_areoles) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L361-L443>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L1–L52: Module docstring mapping equations to code and Lean 4 theorems <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L1-L52>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Implements both Runions et al. (2005) Eq. (1) open Voronoi space colonization (L = 0 loops) and Eq. (2)-(3) exact Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) closed venation with persistent V(s) source tagging, genealogical hop exclusion (tree_hop_distance >= 4, eliminating 3-cycle triangles), and exact planar segment-intersection rejection (segments_properly_intersect, 0 crossing edges, 409 planar loops). Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L148–L224: segments_properly_intersect(), tree_hop_distance(), and exact compute_rng_neighbors() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L148-L224>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L227–L456: simulate_venation(): persistent V(s) source tagging and planar anastomosis closure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L227-L456>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Morphometric validation: 91/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Validates 12 quantitative metrics across open/closed Euler loop counts (L = 0 vs L = 409), exact Murray root-to-tip cubic conductance conservation (r_root^3 = 371.0 = N_tips * r_tip^3), binary junction area ratios across 8 Strahler orders on an explicit 2,175-node tree (r = 0.9679, MAE = 0.0208 vs Price et al. 2013), and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated (358 areoles, i_u = 0.4462) and segmented specimen (168 areoles, i_u = 0.6134) networks. Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L548–L628: build_and_measure_multiscale_strahler_tree(): explicit 8-order tree measured via analyze_junction_scaling() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L548-L628>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L634–L712: compute_planar_areole_nesting_from_raster() and compute_simulated_network_areole_nesting() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L634-L712>; runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): 12-row quantitative metrics CSV — runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py at c89d18d, text/csv, 1360 B, artifact_sha256 6b1d640aaa78f2183c4bff360c7af745f55a6d7c076c4d80435966b6aeaad4fa (sha256 6b1d640aaa78f2183c4bff360c7af745f55a6d7c076c4d80435966b6aeaad4fa), spec_fingerprint 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): open Ginkgo venation anastomosing cycle count L = E - V + 1 = 0 loops (reference 0, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 3 (open venation tree)) [Euler-Poincaré independent cycle rank E - V + 1 on open Voronoi space-colonization tree]; Murray's cube law root-to-tip conservation ratio r_root^3 / (N_tips * r_tip^3) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Murray 1926 PNAS 12:207 / Runions et al. 2005 Sec. 3.5 / Lean 4 theorem murray_1926_tree_conservation) [ratio of petiole root cubic radius r_root^3 to sum of terminal veinlet cubic radii sum r_tip^3] — r_root^3 = 371.0, N_tips = 371; open venation binary junction median daughter/parent area ratio (A_1 + A_2)/A_0 = 1.2439 area ratio (reference 1.2599, Murray 1926 symmetric bifurcation 2^{1/3} = 1.2599 / Price et al. 2013 PLoS ONE e85420 Fig. 3) [median (r_1^2 + r_2^2) / r_0^2 across binary bifurcations of the grown open venation tree]; closed reticulate venation anastomosing loop count L = E - V + 1 = 409 areole loops (reference 150, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 4 Eq. (2)-(3)) [Euler cycle rank E - V + 1 of closed Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) space-colonization network] — V = 1099, E = 1507; Horton-Strahler order 1 vs order 8 median area-ratio shift = 0.1835 delta area ratio (reference 0.24, Price, Knox & Brodribb 2013 PLoS ONE 8(12):e85420 Fig. 4 (order 1 median 1.25 -> order 8 median 1.01)) [decrease in median daughter/parent cross-sectional area ratio from terminal minor veins (order 1) to major midveins (order 8)] — Pearson r across Strahler orders = 0.9679; Katifori & Magnasco (2012) unweighted hierarchical loop nesting number i_u = 0.4462 nesting index i_u (reference 0.68, Katifori & Magnasco 2012 PLoS ONE e37994 / Ronellenfitsch et al. 2015 PLoS Comput. Biol. e1004680 Fig. 3b) [mean subtree partition balance q_j = 1 - |r_j - s_j|/(r_j + s_j - 1) under iterative minimum-width vein removal] — high-noise / additive control i_u = 0.6134; segmented reticulate leaf skeleton specimen areole count = 168 areoles (reference 180, Wikimedia Commons File:Vein skeleton of a leaf (de-ghosted).jpg (CC BY-SA 3.0)) [connected enclosed areole faces segmented directly from datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg] — segmented specimen nesting index i_u = 0.6134, Ginkgo open specimen loops = 0." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-7> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Remediated v2 reproduction of Runions et al. (2005) leaf venation space colonization, Murray (1926) / Price et al. (2013) vascular scaling, and Katifori & Magnasco (2012) loop nesting. Resolves all five v1 audit findings by adding real pixel segmentation of both specimen photographs, persistent V(s) source tagging with genealogical hop exclusion and planar segment-intersection enforcement, planar dual areole extraction for Katifori loop nesting, explicit multiscale Strahler tree junction measurement, and machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 90.1, reproducibility 93.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py at c89d18d, image/png, 1138697 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34 (sha256 d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34), spec_fingerprint 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9; artifact_sha256: d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=c22c5f4e26f3e2c6...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-18-venation-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs; transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks; does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.13e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

